# 🔒 Security Audit Report — News Intelligence Platform

## Audit Results: Before vs. After

---

## ✅ Already Production-Grade (No Changes Required)

| Layer | Status | Details |
|---|---|---|
| **Helmet headers** | ✅ Excellent | CSP, HSTS, frameguard, noSniff, referrer policy — all set |
| **CORS** | ✅ Excellent | Strict origin whitelist, no-origin blocked in prod, 24h preflight cache |
| **MongoSanitize** | ✅ Good | `$` / `.` stripped from all req.body, req.query, req.params |
| **XSS body encoder** | ✅ Good | Recursive HTML-encoding on all body string values |
| **HPP protection** | ✅ Good | Duplicate query params collapsed, whitelist for arrays |
| **Rate limiting tiers** | ✅ Good | 5 tiers (global, auth, AI, search, strict, admin) |
| **JWT expiry/revocation** | ✅ Good | `changedPasswordAfter()` check on every request |
| **Error handler** | ✅ Good | Non-operational errors masked from clients |
| **Body size limit** | ✅ Good | express.json({ limit: '10mb' }) + Content-Length pre-check |

---

## 🔧 Vulnerabilities Fixed

### 1. JWT Algorithm Substitution Attack (Critical)
**Before:**
```typescript
jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET ?? '')
```
**After:**
```typescript
jwt.verify(token, env.JWT_SECRET, {
  algorithms: ['HS256'],        // Pin algorithm
  issuer:     env.JWT_ISSUER,   // Validate iss claim
  audience:   env.JWT_AUDIENCE, // Validate aud claim
})
```
**Risk mitigated:** An attacker who obtains a public key could forge tokens by switching the algorithm to RS256. Pinning to `HS256` and validating `iss`/`aud` claims completely eliminates this attack vector.

### 2. Unvalidated `process.env` in Auth Critical Path (High)
**Before:** `process.env.JWT_SECRET ?? ''` — falls back to empty string if env not loaded  
**After:** `env.JWT_SECRET` — validated at startup, throws if missing

### 3. Internal Error Message Leak (Medium)
**Before:**
```typescript
error = new AppError(err.message, 500, false); // Leaks stack details
```
**After:**
```typescript
error = new AppError('An unexpected error occurred. Our team has been notified.', 500, false);
```
**Risk mitigated:** Programmer errors (e.g., `Cannot read property of undefined`) could reveal internal function names, file paths, and logic to attackers.

### 4. Security Audit Logging Missing (Medium)
**Before:** `console.warn(...)` in mongoSanitize callback  
**After:** `log.warn({ key, ip, method, path, requestId })` — structured, goes to SIEM

### 5. Path Traversal / Prototype Pollution / SQLi (Medium) — New
Added `suspiciousRequestGuard` middleware that rejects requests containing:
- `../../` — path traversal
- `__proto__` / `constructor.prototype` — prototype pollution
- `UNION SELECT` / `OR 1=1` — SQL injection probing
- `%00` / `\x00` — null byte injection
- `${...}` — server-side template injection

### 6. Rate Limit Key Collision (Low)
**Before:** Auth limiter keyed by `email ?? req.ip` (OR logic — easy to bypass)  
**After:** Keyed by `email:ip` (AND — must be same email AND same IP)

### 7. AI Limiter Not User-Aware (Low)
**Before:** AI limiter keyed by IP — corporate NAT means all employees share one limit  
**After:** AI limiter keys by `userId` when authenticated, falls back to IP for guests

---

## 🛡️ Complete Security Architecture

```
Internet
    │
    ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  1. Helmet (HTTP headers)                               │
│     CSP • HSTS • X-Frame-Options • noSniff • XSS       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  2. CORS whitelist (strict origin enforcement)          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  3. Global rate limiter (100 req/15min per IP)          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  4. Body parser (10MB limit)                            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  5. MongoSanitize (strip $ and . from all user input)   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  6. XSS body encoder (HTML-encode all strings)          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  7. HPP protection (deduplicate query params)           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  8. SuspiciousRequestGuard (path traversal, SQLi, etc.) │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  9. Request ID (traceability per request)               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  10. Route-specific limiters                            │
│      Auth: 10/15min (email+IP fingerprint)              │
│      AI:   20/min (by userId when authenticated)        │
│      Search: 30/min                                     │
│      Strict: 5/hour (password reset)                    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  11. express-validator (field-level input validation)   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  12. JWT auth (HS256 pinned, iss+aud validated)         │
│      + changedPasswordAfter() revocation check          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  13. RBAC authorize() (role-based access control)       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  14. Business logic / route handlers                    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  15. Global error handler (errors masked in production) │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 📋 Production Security Checklist

### Environment
- [ ] `JWT_SECRET` ≥ 64 random characters (`openssl rand -base64 64`)
- [ ] `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET` is **different** from `JWT_SECRET`
- [ ] `JWT_ISSUER` and `JWT_AUDIENCE` set to production values
- [ ] `MONGODB_URI` uses a dedicated database user with least-privilege (not root)
- [ ] `OPENAI_API_KEY` has usage limits set in the OpenAI dashboard
- [ ] `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` is set to the exact production frontend URL only
- [ ] `NODE_ENV=production` set (enables HSTS, strict CSP, error masking)
- [ ] All secrets rotated from development values

### Infrastructure
- [ ] HTTPS enforced at load balancer / nginx (not just HSTS header)
- [ ] MongoDB Atlas IP Whitelist contains only backend server IPs
- [ ] Redis protected with a strong password (`REDIS_PASSWORD`)
- [ ] No sensitive env vars in Docker images (use secrets manager)

### Monitoring
- [ ] Failed auth attempts trigger alerts (>5 per minute)
- [ ] Rate limit hits logged to SIEM
- [ ] XSS/injection blocks logged and reviewed weekly
- [ ] Dependency audit: `npm audit --audit-level=high` in CI pipeline
- [ ] Error tracking service configured (Sentry, Datadog, etc.)

### API Security
- [ ] No sensitive data in API responses (no passwords, secrets, internal IDs in errors)
- [ ] Admin endpoints tested to confirm `authorize('admin')` blocks non-admins
- [ ] AI usage endpoint (`/api/v1/ai/usage`) confirmed inaccessible to regular users
- [ ] File upload endpoints (if any) validate MIME type server-side
